-- Independent tests: AI-content labelling (EU Art. 50 + Code Measure 1.1; Washington
-- E2SHB 1170; California Bus. & Prof. Code 22757.x as amended by SB 1000).
--
-- Every expected value here was decided in phase 1, from BRIEF.md and source/ alone,
-- BEFORE this encoding was opened, and is recorded with its reasoning, its provision
-- and the verbatim source text in EXPECTED.md (the independent tester's scratchpad,
-- babel-independent/EXPECTED.md). This file was then written from the encoding's
-- exported NAMES and record SHAPES only; tests-*.l4, census.l4, CENSUS.md and NOTES.md
-- were not read. A failing assertion here is a finding; no expected value was changed
-- to match what the encoding computes.
--
-- Each assertion is preceded by a comment: the EXPECTED.md scenario id, the question
-- (q1a q1b q2 q3a q3b q4a q4b q5, as EXPECTED.md s.2.1), the provisions, and the
-- expected answer. Where EXPECTED.md says "n/a (as carried: X)", X is asserted, since
-- the encoding's marking-quality functions do not depend on the duty. Where it says
-- n/a with no as-carried value, nothing is asserted.
--
-- Records are built here field by field with WITH; test-kit.l4 is not imported.
--
-- READING THE COUNTS. check.sh counts "assertion failed" only where it follows
-- "Message:" on the same line. Two kinds of failure here do not print that way:
--   * `#ASSERT REFUSED e` where e produces a value prints "Message:" and then, on
--     the NEXT line, "assertion failed: expected a refusal, but the expression
--     produced a value". check.sh counts it under errors, not under failed.
--   * `#ASSERT e` where e REFUSES prints "assertion refused" at Warning severity,
--     which check.sh counts nowhere. Where this file expected a value, that is a
--     failed expectation too.
-- Grep the l4 run output for both strings, not only check.sh's columns.
--
-- ======================================================================
-- NOT EXPRESSIBLE with the encoding's names (a coverage finding)
-- ======================================================================
--
-- Whole scenarios not asserted:
--   C-10  (A)-(D) conveyed "through a link to a permanent internet website"
--         (22757.3(a)(1)). The domain has no field for a disclosure conveyed by link,
--         nor for whether the linked site is permanent. Q4b cannot be expressed; the
--         other answers would be B0's on identical inputs.
--   C-11  The same, with a link to a page that expires. Not expressible for the same
--         reason.
--
-- Single questions not asserted (the rest of the scenario is asserted):
--   M-05 q1b, q4b  Signed manifest with no time-stamp although time information was
--         available, while the manifest's assertions still state the creation time.
--         The domain has ONE time field, `the time it records` (signature_info.time),
--         read both as Sub-measure 1.1.1's time-stamp and as 22757.3(a)(1)(C)'s
--         "time and date of the content's creation". The two facts cannot differ. Nor
--         is "time information available on the generating system" a field; the Code
--         module refuses for want of it.
--   M-06 q1b  No time information available on the device. Not a field (see M-05);
--         the encoding refuses where EXPECTED.md says MET.
--   C-06 q1b  Time-stamped signature but no creation time conveyed: the same single
--         time field (see M-05).
--   C-08 q1b  The manifest records that the content is AI-generated but not whether
--         it was created or altered. The domain reads 22757.3(a)(1)(E) and
--         Sub-measure 1.1.1's "record ... whether the content is AI-generated" from
--         the SAME fields (source types, AI-disclosure assertion), so (E) cannot be
--         missing while the 1.1.1 record is present.
--   M-20 q1b  An image exported in a format that cannot carry metadata (EXPECTED.md
--         expects REFUSE, ambiguity A-07). The domain has no field for whether the
--         format supports metadata; every image is treated as able to carry it.
--   M-02, M-20, W-14, P-03 q3b  Whether a watermark follows "a commonly supported
--         technical standard for watermarking" (WA s.2(2)). Not a field; the WA module
--         refuses by design. EXPECTED.md: NOT DEEMED for M-02, M-20 and P-03
--         (proprietary), DEEMED for W-14 (standard).
--
-- Expressed by approximation (asserted; noted so a reader can discount them):
--   M-04, P-19  Unsigned XMP/IPTC metadata. The domain holds only a `C2PA manifest`,
--         so these are entered as a manifest whose signature does not validate.
--         Whether a NON-C2PA metadata standard is "commonly supported" (WA s.2(2)) is
--         not a field; the WA module deems any manifest compliant.
--   M-09, M-10  EXPECTED.md has four facts for the closed-product case (embedded in a
--         physical product; technically controlled and closed environment; mainly
--         instructive; effective measures against the output leaving). The domain has
--         one boolean, `it stays inside a closed physical product`, entered FALSE for
--         both. Which limb fails is not tested.
--   M-12 to M-16  Token counts are not a field; `it is very short text` is entered
--         per the Code's Glossary ("shorter than 200 tokens"): 199 -> TRUE, 200 -> FALSE.
--         The 200-token boundary is therefore tested in this file's inputs, not in the
--         encoding.
--   ED-1 to ED-7  The placement date is a boolean, `its system was placed on the EU
--         market before 2 August 2026`; ED-5 (placed 2 Aug) and ED-6 (placed 1 Aug)
--         are entered FALSE and TRUE. ED-7 (put into service, never placed) is FALSE.
--   P-18  The platform's user count is one number for the preceding 12 months; the
--         peak month, 2,500,000, is entered (EXPECTED.md ambiguity A-26).
--   W-03, W-07  "business-to-business" is a property of the provider record here, not
--         of the use; entered TRUE for both.
--   W-04 to W-06  WA's government limb is one boolean for "state, local, and tribal";
--         the three scenarios differ only in name.
--   E2-03 The Composite system's user count is not stated in EXPECTED.md; 2,000 is
--         entered (it is not covered in Washington either way: not consumer-accessible).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `labelling-domain`
IMPORT `eu-ai-act-art50`
IMPORT `eu-code-of-practice`
IMPORT `wa-e2shb-1170`
IMPORT `ca-bpc-22757`

-- ======================================================================
-- Judgement inputs, named by their values (EXPECTED.md s.2.2)
-- ======================================================================

-- J1 standard editing, J2 does not substantially alter, J3 falsely authentic, J4 evidently artistic
`EU judgements F F F F` MEANS
    `EU Article 50 judgements` WITH
        `the AI system performs an assistive function for standard editing` IS FALSE
        `the AI system does not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof` IS FALSE
        `the content would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful` IS FALSE
        `the content forms part of an evidently artistic, creative, satirical, fictional or analogous work or programme` IS FALSE

-- J1 standard editing, J2 does not substantially alter, J3 falsely authentic, J4 evidently artistic
`EU judgements F F F T` MEANS
