        `including a latent disclosure is technically feasible` IS TRUE
        `the disclosure is permanent or extraordinarily difficult to remove or tamper with` IS TRUE
        `the disclosure is compatible with the covered provider's disclosure verification tool` IS TRUE

-- Article 50(4) answers, short names
`FULL disclosure` MEANS `disclosure that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated`
`LIMITED disclosure` MEANS `disclosure of the existence of such generated or manipulated content, in a manner that does not hamper the display or enjoyment of the work`
`NO disclosure` MEANS `no disclosure under Article 50(4)`

